    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78">

                <pb facs="0346" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg60"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2981</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Saloniki</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kehl</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Saloniki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-10-24T17:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 24, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 25, 12.30 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your October 21, 5 p. m. Shall act in accordance with my telegram of October 13,
                    1 p. m. Minister of Finance Provisional authorities has written that he
                    considered Consulate’s relations informal and unofficial, and expressed
                    intention of asking Government of United States for official recognition in near
                    future.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consul</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
